Operator option 2: study github.com/DriesSmit/ARC3-solution (ARC-AGI-3 preview winner, Tufa Labs)
and report what's borrowable. Cloned to /tmp (NOT the repo tree), read in full (~882 LOC).

VERDICT: nothing borrowable that Carnot lacks. The winner's agent is a frame-change-prediction CNN
that biases exploration -- component-by-component already in Carnot:
- ActionModel (CNN + click-heatmap + conv coord head)  == arc_frame_change_predictor.SmallFrameChangeCNN (exp4490/4547)
- online supervised learning + 200K hash-dedup buffer    == arc_online_action_effect_scorer (exp4710/4726)
- dynamic model+buffer reset on new level                == arc_online_action_effect_scorer.reset() (clears buffer + Adam, restores prior)
- conv 2D coordinate head                                == arc_live_ttt conv per-cell heads
- exploration biased toward predicted-change actions     == exp4629 action-effect CNN + PersistentAEM (BANKED efficiency 2.0->1.0)

DECISIVE CONVERGENCE: Carnot's instances reached the winner's exact outcome -- exp4629 efficiency-up
but NO first-win lift; exp4710/4726 online-learning NULLED for first-win -- mirroring StochasticGoose's
12.58% preview -> 0.25% unseen collapse (arXiv:2603.24621). Two independent teams, same architecture,
same wall. The winner has no generation/first-win lever because nobody does.

Micro-deltas (CNN depth, pure-conv coord head) are secondary; Carnot's clicks already land <=2px of
centroids (guidance_not_coverage), so EV ~0. No generation lever to borrow.

VALUE: confirms Carnot is at architectural parity with the frontier preview-winner (0.08 is not a gap
to a known-better method) + convergent independent confirmation of the WALL_IS_HIDDEN_STATE closure.
Option 2 closes with no code to borrow; deliverable stands (0.08 + FoVer paper).

